        "text": "This will create a compressed file named app.log.gz in the same /var/log/ directory:\nFigure 3.4 \u2013 Compressed app.log.gz file from 1 GB to 1.0 MB\n\u2022 A system administrator wants to compress a directory named backup located in the /home/\ninstructor directory. This directory compression process is often referred to as creating a\n\u201ctarball,\u201d which is a common method for bundling and compressing multiple files or directories\ninto a single archive file. The administrator can use the following command to compress the\nbackup directory:\nFigure 3.5 \u2013 Compressing a directory called backup.tar.gz\nThis will create a compressed file named backup.tar.gz in the same directory. The tar\ncommand will also be introduced for our next topic. The czvf option supplied in the preceding\ncommand is used to create a compressed archive in gzip format.\nThe options are as follows:\nI Create an archive\nI Compress the archive using gzip\nI Display progress information\nI Specify the name of the archive file\ntar, rar, and unrar\n55",
